bnet slots. The orchestrator setup requirements give no GPU, memory, CPU or disk minimum and list no mandatory paid service. The registration example sets the orchestrator\u2019s fee to 10%.","Beam calculates confidence separately for standard and room transfers, with targets of 120 and 40 verified original tasks respectively. It compares the fraction of accountable tasks each miner completes successfully, and if both rates are zero, the miners draw. If positive rates tie and both completion times are available and finite, the faster miner wins unless the slower time is within 5% of the faster time, in which case they draw.","For pay, Beam ranks qualified miners by verified uploads. Each MiB counts at 1\u00d7 for the top 30, then at 0.8\u00d7, 0.2\u00d7 and 0.08\u00d7 for successive groups of 30, and at 0.0075\u00d7 thereafter. Fraud-report bonuses, sales, redistribution and penalties adjust those shares.","The code reads the number of blocks per epoch from the chain, and the orchestrator registration instructions give no registration protection period. Read from https://github.com/Beam-Network/beam at commit 79a536e on 2026-11-23."],"how_it_was_made":"This note was put together by AI agents and not by a person who mines here. One agent read the subnet's public repository and wrote down what a miner does, what it takes and how the work is paid, with a source for each statement, and a second agent opened every source and took out whatever it did not support. Of 29 source checks, 12 held, 2 did not hold and 15 could not be opened, and only what held is in the text above. Nothing of the subnet's code was run, and the note describes the code as it stood on the day and at the commit named in its last sentence, so it can be out of date.","page":"https://check.loopholetape.com/mine/105.html"},"read_until":"2026-11-26T12:05:36Z","weeks":[{"entered_from":"2026-10-27","entered_to":"2026-10-29","entries":70,"wallets":42,"typical_fee_usd":2.09,"earning_after_7_days":6,"counted_